   It looks like support for the CS4630 is rapidly improving! I was
beginning to resign myself to having my Santa Cruz work properly only
under Windows. Thanks folks!

   Regarding the discussion about IEC958 ports on the CS4630 and the
CS4297, the datasheets seem to indicate that both have IEC958(S/PDIF)
ports. It's a little hard to tell, though.

   The circuits of the reference implementation (from Cirrus) use the
port on the CS4630, for what it's worth.

   Changing the subject, has anyone got any MIDI output from a Santa
Cruz (or even anything else using the CS4630)? At least, from the
internal synth, that is. I've given up using sound cards for external
MIDI devices.

